{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>To the goats.</b> They are the demons, and they are called so because the body that sees them bristles, and the near one, because the madmen see them in the likeness of goats. And the word \"anymore\" is according to the way Israel used to do in Egypt." "<b>Who prostitute themselves.</b> For everyone who seeks them and believes in them is a prostitute beneath his Elohim, in that he thinks there is someone who can do good or evil besides HaShem, the honored and awesome One. And in this passage he did not mention the stranger, because the commandment is upon Israel regarding offerings and burnt offerings. And he mentioned the stranger so that Israel not let the stranger slaughter to idolatry in the land of Israel. And likewise the law of all blood that is forbidden, because it is the life, for the flesh is in the blood. And the truth is that the life by which a man lives is in the blood of the heart."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Resolved the ambiguous והקרוב as 'the near one' (i.e., one who approaches them); the wordplay on שעיר/משתער is rendered literally without explanatory expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:36.688814753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}